Package: okpal
Title: OKLAB/OKLCH-Based Perceptual Color Interpolation and Colorblind-Safe Palette Generation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jun-yeong", "Heo", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "fleatinum@gmail.com")
Description: Attempt to provide perceptually uniform color gradients by interpolating 
    in OKLAB/OKLCH color spaces via the 'farver' package, avoiding the muddy 
    mid-tones caused by RGB interpolation. Also includes tools for generating, 
    adjusting, and checking colorblind-safe palettes using CVD simulation 
    from 'colorspace'. Provides ready-to-use scale functions for 'ggplot2', 
    'pheatmap', and 'ComplexHeatmap'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Imports:
    farver (>= 2.1.0),
    colorspace,
    ggplot2,
    grDevices
Suggests:
    pheatmap,
    ComplexHeatmap,
    circlize,
    patchwork,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
